Never use dark: css classes. Rely on CSS variables set in tailwind for dark mode
avoid using tailwind colors like green or red, pay attention to globals.css and pick proper color classes based on Tailwind 4 and ShadCDN 2.6 standards
avoid using shadows and borders as much as possible. neat clean UI
prefer JSDoc comments
Be aware the app support RTL and LTR directions. use ms instead of ml in tailwind classes and so on
use pnpm
after changes run `pnpm tsc` to ensure no type errors are found
you can use the following tools:
    getConsoleLogs
    getConsoleErrors
    getNetworkErrors
    getNetworkLogs
    takeScreenshot
    getSelectedElement
    wipeLogs
    runAccessibilityAudit
    runPerformanceAudit
    runSEOAudit
    runNextJSAudit
    runDebuggerMode
    runAuditMode
    runBestPracticesAudit

use above tools to make sure there are no runtime errors after making changes 